  "slug": "cosmic-dark-d878",
  "summary": "Four preprints sharpen dark-sector and early-Universe model tests via UV bounds, Boltzmann treatments, axion abundance and flavor-testable flavons.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a focus on stress-testing early-Universe and dark-sector scenarios against consistency conditions or experimental reach. Dirac leptogenesis is extended to charged leptons in a Froggatt-Nielsen setup, with a 1.7-50 GeV flavon testable through lepton flavor observables. UV-complete models are used to bound inflationary parity violation from dynamical Chern-Simons terms, with strong bispectrum constraints. Higgs-portal dark matter near resonance is revisited by solving the momentum-dependent Boltzmann equation, which indicates that standard treatments are inadequate beyond kinetic equilibrium. Multi-component axion dark matter with stochastic mixing allows QCD axions or ultralight ALPs to dominate the abundance and enlarges the allowed QCD axion parameter space. The new element is more rigorous treatment of each model's assumptions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
